For developers

XML input and learner-selected dimensions
Use &lt;input&gt;&lt;type&gt;matrix&lt;/type&gt;... for a fixed-size matrix; the input model answer supplies its dimensions. For learner-selected columns, as in the basis examples, add:
&lt;matrix&gt;
  &lt;rows initial="3" min="3" max="3" resizable="0"/&gt;
  &lt;cols initial="1" min="1" max="3" resizable="1"/&gt;
&lt;/matrix&gt;
Each axis requires initial, min, max and resizable. A fixed axis uses resizable="0" with equal initial, minimum and maximum. The product of the two maxima may not exceed 64. This sizing element is a STACK SymPy extension and needs adaptation for native Moodle STACK. The input model and authored tests must fit the configured dimensions. For a matrix-defined space, the input model can use nullspace_basis(A), columnspace_basis(A) or rowspace_basis(A) while the PRT uses the original A.


Supported values and tests
Author expressions write a matrix as matrix([a,b],[c,d]), distinct from a nested list. Matrices must be rectangular and complete, with 1–16 rows and columns and at most 64 scalar entries. Cells cannot contain collections, equations or logical values. The supported native STACK matrix tests here are AlgEquiv, SameType and EqualComAss; other native matrix tests and general matrix arithmetic are outside this port’s current support.
Raw cells remain unchanged until validation interprets them. The editor does not create zeros for blank cells or compute marks. The reusable component and its provenance are recorded in the project source tree; question authors configure it through XML.

For teachers
These are 35 unchanged STACK XML questions from the upstream library. The 23 questions whose authored tests passed on every replayed seed have interactive cards. Each question has a local XML download and an observed result. One additional presentation teaching copy shows a matrix question whose original HTML is unsupported. Other originals remain available with the observed mismatch or unsupported feature shown explicitly.
In this snapshot, 23 pass their author tests, 1 has a test mismatch, and 11 cannot be fully checked here. The replay record gives the tested variants and exact results.
The worked matrix examples also include a determinant-one task and two basis questions. The SPD example adds a custom Python checker. These Python tests are separate from these unchanged exports and their baseline counts. See Python answer tests.

