    &lt;questiontext format="html"&gt;
      &lt;text&gt;&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p&gt;Given that \(\ln(a)={@a@}\) , express: \[\log_{a}(x^{@n@})\] as a single multiple of a natural logarithm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;\(\log_{a}(x^{@ n @}) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]&lt;/p&gt;]]&gt;&lt;/text&gt;
    &lt;/questiontext&gt;
    &lt;generalfeedback format="html"&gt;
      &lt;text&gt;&lt;![CDATA[&lt;p&gt;Below are the basic rules of logarithms.&lt;br /&gt;\[\log_{b}(mn) = \log_{b}(m) +\log_{b}(n)\]&lt;br /&gt;\[\log_{b}\left(\frac{m}{n}\right) = \log_{b}(m) -\log_{b}(n)\]&lt;br /&gt;\[\log_{b}(m^n) = n\cdot\log_{b}(m)\]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;\[\log_{a}(m)=\frac{\log_{b}(m)}{\log_{b}(a)}\]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Hence \[\log_{a}(x^{@n@}) = {@n@}\log_{a}(x) = {@n@}\frac{\ln(x)}{\ln(a)}\]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;\[ = {@n@}\frac{\ln(x)}{@a@}={@correctanswer@}\]&lt;/p&gt;]]&gt;&lt;/text&gt;
    &lt;/generalfeedback&gt;
    &lt;defaultgrade&gt;1&lt;/defaultgrade&gt;
    &lt;penalty&gt;0&lt;/penalty&gt;
